    "sections": [
      {
        "type": "text",
        "content": "Sam Peckinpah's The Getaway revolutionized the heist film genre by infusing raw violence with complex character dynamics. Steve McQueen and Ali MacGraw's electric chemistry powers this gritty crime thriller that influenced countless later films like <a href=\"/movie/949\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"949\">Heat</a> (1995) and <a href=\"/movie/338766\" class=\"movie-title\" data-tmdb-id=\"338766\">Hell or High Water</a> (2016). Peckinpah's signature balletic violence and innovative editing techniques - particularly in the hotel shootout sequence - created a template for modern action cinematography that directors like John Woo and Quentin Tarantino would later reference."
      },
      {
